Subject: Cantor Candidate Seal and Independent Review Boundary Assessment

Description: Non-authoritative design assessment for turning a stopped disposable candidate into reviewable immutable evidence without allowing the mutating worker to certify or promote itself.

& [AssessmentIdentity] is a local architecture review
  + [assessment_uuid] is f3dff46f-0c69-4da2-9992-bb478245c3dd
  + [captured_at] is 2026-07-30
  + [status] is sufficient_for_formation_not_implementation

& [CoreFinding] is that seal, test, and review are different trust transitions
  + [seal] answers what physical candidate state was captured
  + [test] answers what exact supervisor-selected executions observed on a reconstruction
  + [review] answers whether evidence satisfies the commission strongly enough for later promotion consideration
  + [promotion] remains a fourth transition outside Phase3C
  - never: collapse integrity, behavior, judgment, and effect authorization into one success flag

& [ConsistencyFinding] is that a directory walk is not inherently a snapshot
  + [risk] is a lingering process can alter bytes between inventory and hashing
  + [minimum_gate] is Phase3B child and descendant quiescence plus two bounded equivalent physical inventories around capture
  + [stronger_future_gate] is an OS or filesystem snapshot primitive proven on the target host
  + [honesty] is equal inventories reduce detected drift but do not prove that no transient external writer existed between observations
  + [record] must name the achieved consistency class and its residual uncertainty
  + [failure_semantics] is any drift quarantines the candidate and invalidates the attempted capsule

& [RepositoryFinding] is that Git status is necessary but insufficient
  + [Git_strength] is canonical base, ref, index, tracked, untracked, ignored, and mode comparison
  + [Git_limit] is it does not independently prove every current filesystem byte, alias, special file, or out-of-tree target
  + [direct_strength] is exact path normalization, file-kind inspection, byte length, streaming SHA-256, and optional bounded byte capture
  + [reconciliation] is Git and direct inventory must agree on the entire admitted change set

& [IndexFinding] is that candidate staging is forbidden
  + [reason] is Phase3B has no Git-history or index mutation authority
  + [gate] is the candidate index tree must still equal the exact base tree
  + [result] is the capsule describes worktree changes relative to base without inheriting a worker-curated staging area

& [IgnoredFileFinding] is that ignored additions remain effects
  + [risk] is ordinary status output may hide generated, secret, or malicious files
  + [gate] is ignored and untracked records are inventoried explicitly and reconciled with a bounded direct walk
  + [policy] is any undeclared ignored or out-of-policy path quarantines

& [CapsuleFinding] is that a hash alone is not durable review material
  + [manifest] binds upstream receipts, run record, repository invariants, path records, byte digests, content references, capture resources, and faults
  + [blobs] preserve exact changed regular-file bytes under digest-derived identities
  + [publication] requires private staging, full read-back verification, atomic final naming, and collision equality
  + [signature] proves which admitted sealer captured which capsule but does not approve contents
  + [immutability] is content-addressed tamper evidence unless a separately proven platform primitive makes the storage physically immutable

& [TestFinding] is that tests commonly mutate their workspace
  + [risk] is build output can contaminate the source seal or test scripts can escape
  + [boundary] is seal source first, reconstruct elsewhere, run an exact supervisor plan under separately proven containment, and retain its record separately
  + [honesty] is a passing test proves only the declared execution under the captured environment
  + [blocker] is test-runner sandbox and reconstruction formation before implementation

& [ReviewFinding] is that independence is structural rather than rhetorical
  + [minimum] is a separate deterministic verifier with immutable input and no candidate-write or promotion capability
  + [model_review] may add semantic criticism through a new read-only context but cannot override failed deterministic gates
  + [output] is eligibility for later consideration, not current authority
  + [uncertainty] must survive as explicit unresolved findings

& [RecommendedStateMachine] is one-way
  + [Admitted] moves to Quiescent only after exact-process closure
  + [Quiescent] moves to Capturing only after repository and filesystem preflight
  + [Capturing] moves to Sealed only after complete digest and publication verification
  + [Sealed] moves to Tested only through a separate reconstruction and test capability
  + [Tested] moves to Reviewed only through an independent reviewer
  + [any_fault] moves to Quarantined or Unresolved without cleanup
  + [Reviewed] may only hand an immutable decision to Phase3D

& [ImplementationBlockers] are explicit
  + [blocker_1] is exact cross-platform path, link, special-file, mode, ignored-file, and inventory grammar
  + [blocker_2] is target-host quiescence and snapshot-consistency proof
  + [blocker_3] is seal-root admission, atomic publication, durability, permissions, and collision contract
  + [blocker_4] is deterministic reconstruction from base plus exact capsule
  + [blocker_5] is separately contained supervisor-test runner and malicious-test fixtures
  + [blocker_6] is independent-review criteria, provenance, and Phase3D handoff contract
